      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Why did amateurism last so long?",
          "Class preservation mechanism + IOC/governing body self-interest; collapsed when money exceeded the social cost of enforcing fiction"
        ],
        [
          "What ended tennis amateurism (1968)?",
          "Best players were all pro, Grand Slams had second-tier talent; embarrassment was unsustainable"
        ],
        [
          "What ended rugby union amateurism (1995)?",
          "Murdoch's $550M Super League offer threatened the talent base"
        ],
        [
          "What ended Olympic amateurism (1992)?",
          "IOC ceded eligibility to individual federations; Dream Team was the visible marker"
        ],
        [
          "What established baseball free agency?",
          "Messersmith arbitration (1975) via CBA mechanism, not legislation or courts"
        ],
        [
          "What is the Bosman ruling?",
          "ECJ 1995: out-of-contract EU players cannot be held by transfer fee; no EU nationality quotas"
        ],
        [
          "Why do TV rights keep inflating despite cord-cutting?",
          "Live sports is DVR-proof — last category where ads can't be skipped; share of live viewership increases as scripted TV fragments"
        ],
        [
          "Why are sports franchises valued at 8-10× revenue?",
          "Supply scarcity (fixed number of franchises), rights inflation secular tailwind, US tax advantages, trophy asset psychology"
        ],
        [
          "What is the Jordan brand model vs. endorsement?",
          "Platform (royalties + equity in a sub-brand that outlasts career) vs. endorser (license image to existing brand)"
        ],
        [
          "Why did the Super League collapse in 48 hours?",
          "UEFA controlled international competition eligibility — players at ESL clubs would miss World Cup/Euros; incumbent platform held the key resource"
        ],
        [
          "What is NIL (2021)?",
          "Name, Image, Likeness rights for US college athletes — overturned 100yr NCAA amateurism via Alston v. NCAA SCOTUS ruling"
        ],
        [
          "What is shamateurism?",
          "Athletes receiving payments (trust funds, expenses, appearance fees) while officially classified as amateur; IAAF trust fund era 1982-1992 is the clearest example"
        ],
        [
          "How does the Moneyball thesis work?",
          "Market inefficiency: when scouts misprice certain statistics, players with those skills trade below market value; edge disappears when market corrects"
        ],
        [
          "What is the WADA zero-day problem?",
          "Testing can only detect known substances; novel designer compounds are undetectable until a sample is analyzed and a test developed — attacker always has a window"
        ]
      ]
    }
